# Test environment template — committed to the repo.
# Copy to .env.test (gitignored) and uncomment/adjust as needed.
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.test.example .env.test
#   source .env.test && <test command>
#
# Note: TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED is already baked into the
# `test` and `test:integration` scripts in server/world-api/package.json,
# so `pnpm test` and `pnpm --filter @aie-matrix/server-world-api test`
# work out of the box without sourcing this file.
# This file is only needed when running tests via a custom command or IDE runner.
#
# Background:
#   Integration tests in server/world-api use testcontainers to spin up a
#   real Neo4j container. On Podman (the default on Apple Silicon dev machines),
#   the Ryuk cleanup daemon's log stream closes before emitting the "Started"
#   message that testcontainers waits for, blocking every container start.
#   Disabling Ryuk is the officially documented Podman workaround; containers
#   are still cleaned up by the test process on normal exit.
#
#   Do NOT set DOCKER_HOST — testcontainers auto-discovers the Podman socket
#   correctly; setting DOCKER_HOST explicitly to /var/run/docker.sock causes
#   container startup to hang until the test timeout (185s).
#
# Docker Desktop users do not need either variable.

# --- Testcontainers / Podman ---
# TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=true
